WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Good to have you here. We're looking at a case today where the people involved were doing

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:11.120
their best with the information they had. In the summer of 2009, dealership lots across the

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.280
United States filled with older sedans and trucks that owners had driven in for the last time.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.140
Under the car allowance rebate system, mechanics drained the oil, ran the engines until they seized,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.920
and then crushed the vehicles so they could never return to the road.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.100
The policy had been written to stimulate auto sales and improve fuel economy during the recession.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.160
Instead, he removed a large slice of the cheapest, reliable transportation from the market

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:46.920
that low income households relied on. The program originated in the depths of the 2008 to 2009

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:53.480
financial crisis, when new vehicle sales had fallen more than 30% from their 2007 peak.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.860
Congressional leaders and the incoming Obama administration saw the auto sector as both an

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:06.620
economic engine and a source of emissions that could be reduced quickly. Lawmakers drew on earlier

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.660
state-level cash for clunkers, pilots, and European scrapage schemes that appeared to boost sales

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:18.820
and fleet turnover. They believed a temporary federal incentive would restart factory lines,

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:26.360
support roughly 150,000 jobs tied to assembly and parts, and delivery immediate environmental gains

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:32.620
by replacing older, less efficient engines. The legislation therefore offered fixed rebates of

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:41.220
3,500 or $4,500 to consumers who traded in vehicles, meeting age and mileage thresholds for newer

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.620
models that achieved at least 22 miles per gallon combined. At the time, the trade-off seems

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:53.360
straightforward. Short-term spending would produce both macroeconomic stimulus and a cleaner vehicle

00:01:53.360 --> 00:02:01.040
stock. President Obama signed the Consumer Assistance to Recycle and Save Act on June 24, 2009,

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.380
allocating $1 billion initially and later adding another $2 billion after the first

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:13.340
tranche ran out in days. The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration opened the program on

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:20.120
July 24, and closed it on August 24, once funds were exhausted. Dealers processed more than

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:28.420
677,000 transactions in that single month, far exceeding forecasts. Contemporary press coverage

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:33.300
showed lines of trade-ends stretching around blocks in cities from Detroit to Phoenix,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.280
and administration officials cited the surge in August new vehicle sales as early proof of concept.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.680
A handful of economists and used-car dealers warned in congressional hearings

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:50.120
that removing so many older vehicles at once could tighten supply in the secondary market.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.780
Those cautions received limited attention amid the focus on immediate job support.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:04.240
Because every accepted trade-in had to be rendered permanently inoperable, roughly 677,000 cars

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:10.780
and light trucks left the used vehicle pool in a matter of weeks. Many of those vehicles still had

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:16.420
years of service life remaining and would normally have been resold multiple times to successive lower

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:23.260
income buyers. With that inventory gone, dealers and private sellers face reduced supply while demand

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:30.460
from budget-conscious households stayed constant or rose. Used car prices rose measurably. Studies

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:36.460
later estimated increases of 6 to 10 percent for the most common models that had qualified as clunkers.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:43.560
Low-income families who had planned to purchase a $3,000 to $5,000 used vehicle found themselves either

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:50.200
priced out or forced to stretch for higher mileage or less reliable alternatives. The program also pulled

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.700
forward purchases that would have occurred anyway, so the net addition to the total fleet was smaller

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:01.780
than the headline transaction counts suggested. Emissions benefits proved modest once researchers

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:07.300
accounted for the manufacturing footprint of the new vehicles and the fact that many buyers chose

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:13.560
larger models that met the mileage threshold only narrowly. The destruction of the trade-ins

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.860
therefore created a lasting scarcity at the bottom of the market rather than a temporary disruption.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:25.480
After the program ended, no follow-on federal scrapage effort of similar scale was attempted.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:31.860
Subsequent academic analyses, including work by resources for the future and the Congressional

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:37.540
Research Service, documented the price effects on used vehicles and the limited long-term stimulus.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:44.140
Some states explored smaller targeted replacements but none repeated the nationwide crushing

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:50.700
requirement. The episode quietly informed later incentive designs which more often relied on repair

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:57.980
subsidies or targeted rebates that left older cars in circulation. Today, the United States used

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:05.000
vehicle market remain sensitive to supply shocks, a vulnerability visible again during the 2021 to

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:13.040
2023 semiconductor shortage when prices for older models climbed sharply. Incentive programs that

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.480
remove durable goods from secondary markets can shift costs onto the very households they aim to

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:25.440
help indirectly. When the mechanism requires permanent destruction rather than resale or refurbishment,

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:30.500
the supply reduction can persist long after the original stimulus window closes.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:36.720
Policy makers weighing similar fleet turnover ideas today might therefore examine whether the

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:42.560
same environmental or economic goals can be reached without eliminating the lowest cost segment of the

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.480
existing stock. How might current electric vehicle purchase incentives interact with the used

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:55.380
market once early models begin to age out? That wraps today's case. The lessons travel further

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:00.620
when you share them. Send this episode to someone who'd find it useful. We'll see you tomorrow.

